    When checking if a node can be deferred, the scheduler will now check the liveness of any registers defined on exit from the loop
    If a node is live-in for the loop exit block then it cannot be safely deferred
    The conflict checker can now check for conflicts across the back-edge of the loop. Some conflicts may have a larger cycle range than the length of the loop, in which case it will move across the back-edge more than once
