Author: Ferran Pallarès Roca <ferran.pallares.roca@intel.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 20 22:47:11 2021 +0100

    Fix corner case for test-runner timeout command-line option
    
    When the value provided by the timeout command-line option was equal to
    the default timeout value, it wasn't possible to know that a
    command-line override had been provided. Thus the timeout value read
    from the test metadata was used.
    
    This commit deals with the previous scenario by reading the default
    timeout value directly into CONF.DEFAULT_META and reserving CONF.TIMEOUT
    for the command-line option alone. This way, when CONF.TIMEOUT is not
    set, we know that the command-line argument wasn't provided.
    
    In addition, treat --skip-higher-timeout-tests option as a 'driver'
    command-line option as opposed to 'test metadata'.

commit 6edb1831e67061e26ee768bffe73494908f9b692
Author: Ferran Pallarès Roca <ferran.pallares.roca@intel.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 18 13:59:49 2021 +0100

    Fix test-runner timeout command-line option
    
    Test metadata is currently sourced from the following places (in
    increasing order of precedence):
      - Default metadata (default.cfg)
      - Command-line options
      - Directory hierarchy CONFIG.txt files
      - Test file itself
    
    This renders the command-line options useless whenever a value is
    specified in the test or CONFIG.txt files.
    
    This commit makes command-line options --timeout and
    --skip-higher-timeout-tests take precedence over the values specified
    in those files.

