    Fix for bug #32780
    When moving instructions across basic block boundaries, the post-RA scheduler didn't consider if a downstream successor node contained a PEU instruction. In these cases, the eventual successor would get moved into another basic block because of its predecessors and may need predication. This isn't possible since the PEU is already in use, so an assertion was hit. The scheduler now tracks downstream PEU usage, so it won't move a node beyond a basic block boundary if it means another non-predicable node will also get moved.

