    Bug #32141 - Adding support for __builtin_prefetch
    When __builtin_prefetch is used, moviCompile will generate an LSU.CPFL1 instruction with the specified pointer.
    The post-RA scheduler will ignore the latency of prefetch instructions and instead move any prefetch to the top of its parent basic block (as it exists when the instruction is being scheduled). It does this to maximise the distance between the prefetch and a corresponding load without increasing the schedule size.

