    First pass at bug #31587. The average execution time for moviCompile in our test-suite has been reduced by ~19%.
    There are some small changes to the SchedulerBase class to use std::unordered_set in place of std::vector wherever strict ordering is not required. I've also added a new field "blockNumber" to SHAVECycleIterator to simplify the comparison operators which are used extensively when looking up maps that use SHAVECycleIterator as a key.
    The major improvement in performance here comes from changes to the ConflictTable which is used to find inter-instruction conflicts in the pre-RA and post-RA schedulers. The functional unit and predication conflicts have been removed from the ConflictTable and are now manually checked in the schedulers first. If one of these conflicts is detected, the "findConflicts" function exits early and does not check the full conflict table. These two conflicts are by far the two most common conflicts detected during scheduling and they are the only conflict types that we can avoid using instruction mutations, which is why we special case them. We only check the full conflictTable when these first two conflicts are not present.

