    Fix for bug #29826.
    The scheduler is now able to move any instructions in a basic block from cycle (1,0) to cycle (0,6) across the branch boundary, with the exception of instructions which load the label for the second branch. Previously, any nodes in a chain which modified i0 were prevented from having their starting cycle moved across this boundary. This caused instructions which were dependent on one another to have overlapping lifetimes.

