Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Wed Mar 14 09:36:30 2018 +0000

    Adding a new vectorizer.
    This is an SLP-based vectorizer which incorporates several other optimizations to target image convolutions and convolution-like functions. It provides:
     * Basic block level vectorization with support for the instruction types BinaryOperator, LoadInst, StoreInst, CastInst, SelectInst, CmpInst and the intrinsic Intrinsic::ctpop.
     * Reordering of chains of associative and commutative operations to restructure data dependencies to allow vertical vectorization
     * Restructuring of loops to allow re-use of overlapping data between iterations (using a form of software pipelining called loop shifting)
     * Tentative loop unrolling to create SLP vectorization opportunities in loop bodies
    Each optimization is discretely enabled/disabled using command-line options defined in MixedVectorizer.cpp
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@139206 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

