commit 75b75469867ee25ce833efcfc1568d5ba87d2def
Author: Martin J. O'Riordan <martin.oriordan@movidius.com>
Date:   Fri Feb 2 13:20:17 2018 +0000

    Disabling one of our questionable changes to the target-independent LLVM sources.
    
    In this case we had altered the default look-unroll handling, and it is not clear that we need to.
    
    Against the MvCV kernels which we are using for performance gating, 8 of the naive implementations experience are massive performance benefit by reverting to the LLVM default, and three others were faster.  Only two of the naive implementations experienced a performance reduction, and only by a tiny amount.  The tuned implementations did not suffer at all.
    
    In my opinion this change does not prove its worth - if anything it looks bad when measured against the MvCV kernels.
    
    I have left the code in, but inverted the 'MOVIDIUS_FIXME' condition to restore the LLVM default, and added an explanation of my findings in the comment.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@135631 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

