commit 20bb9ae09a01c102096fc951a4c6d2f6d12f6633
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Mon Apr 24 12:17:10 2017 +0000

    Reducing the excessive compilation times reported in bug #26687. Compilation of the attached file now takes ~25 seconds. Similarly, the attachment from bug #26715 now compiles in ~82 seconds.
    There are two main changes to the schedulers' dependency graph generator which reduce the compilation time for tests which include a very high number of memory accesses.
    The first is the introduction of the map "latestOutputDependencies". For any node, this map provides a way of tracking the most recent, or nearest predecessor of that node. When there are a high number of memory accesses which may alias each other, this map enables generation of a single chain of nodes, instead of a web of nodes with a high number of edges. This simplifies the dependency graph, reducing the scheduling time.
    The second change introduces a limit to the number of memory accesses which are tracked during dependency graph generation. When the limit is exceeded, the "oldest" memory access is popped off the list and is added to a chain of nodes that were previously popped off the list. The head of this chain is added as a successor for each memory accessing node that follows. This can make the dependency graph slightly more complicated, but it greatly reduces the time it takes to generate the graph.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@121967 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

