    Fixing a bug in the post-RA scheduler which caused non-deterministic code generation in certain cases. When The weight of two blocks were the exact same, they were inserted onto the priority list in the order they happened to be in in the original weight map. The ordering in the weight map is dependent on the value of the basic blocks' pointers. With this fix, they will be inserted depending on their block numbers, which should be the same on each run.
    
