commit 5a23954faba0a017fe930a2dd8e842b8d469aca2
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Wed Jan 11 14:30:09 2017 +0000

    Changing how the weight of dependency graph nodes is calculated during scheduling. Two sets of nodes are generated for each node in the graph. One set is for output dependent nodes for the current node and the other for anti-dependent nodes. The latencies of output dependent nodes are summed to generate the current node's weight. The number of anti-dependent nodes is added to the weight as well.
    This new method has the benefit of adding the latency of each node only once, even if there are multiple paths through the graph to a node.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@115390 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

