    Adding 4 new command-line options for modifying the post-RA scheduler. These are intended primarily to make it easier to find the "best" default settings for different aspects of the scheduler.
    The options "-shave-postra-scheduler-inner-loop-block-weight-modifier" and "-shave-postra-scheduler-outer-loop-block-weight-modifier" can be used to force the scheduler to prefer scheduling of inner or outer loops by modifying the weights assigned to basic blocks in each.
    The scheduler generates traces by picking the basic block with the highest weight in a function and then "growing" the trace in both directions through that block's predecessors and successors. The option "-shave-postra-scheduler-trace-generation-direction" can be used to force the traces to grow in only one direction. The default behaviour is both directions.
    The options "-shave-postra-scheduler-functional-unit-mutation-order" accepts a string which specifies the order in which functional units should be selected when mutating CMU copy instructions. The default order is LSU0,LSU1,IAU,SAU,VAU
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@112561 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

