    Adding a new function to the scheduler base class which checks if a memory load is from a read-only region of memory. If a load is read-only then there cannot be a read-after-write or write-after-read conflict with any store instructions. This is used when building the dependency graphs.
    Fixing a few bugs in the post-RA scheduler.
    When mutating PEU predicate instructions, the new instructions were not being bundled with the other instructions in the bundle.
    When applying instruction mutations, the map of instructions to nodes was not being updated.
    Saurabh discovered a typo I had made which caused the function "scheduleGraph" to continuously reorder the successors of the starting node rather than the current node being scheduled. This is now fixed, and I've also renamed the argument passed to scheduleGraph to prevent any confusion in future.
    When predicating nodes for inter-block movement, CMU compare instructions for the block that is being moved into would end up with new predecessors in the graph. This invalidated the generated order for the workList so I have added an extra check for all predecessors of currentNode to be complete before scheduling that node.
    Finally, adding a new array for tracking basic blocks which use jump tables to branch to their successors. Nodes which require predication to be moved into these blocks cannot be moved since there is no compare instruction to use for the predicate.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@112456 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

