commit 2598fb1345de6f1002f0d818706e86bcc8c81d65
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 28 11:25:46 2016 +0000

    Various changes affecting the behaviour of both the pre-RA and post-RA instruction schedulers.
    For both schedulers, volatile memory accesses (both reads and writes) are treated as sequence points in the schedule. All instructions before a volatile access will now fully complete before the access starts executing and all instructions after a volatile access will now only start executing once the access has completed.
    The post-RA scheduler now performs more aggressive code motion between basic blocks. Instructions are duplicated in the appropriate blocks when moving past an edge in the control flow graph.
    Also removing the top-down scheduler from the post-RA scheduler. The top-down and bottom-up schedulers won't play nice together in the "middle" of the trace being scheduled.
    
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@110485 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

