Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 14 09:22:02 2016 +0000

    Making big changes to how the dependency graphs are generated. Each generated node now tracks a limited set of nodes that can be reached through some path in the graph, starting with one of the node's successors. This helps to reduce the number of redundant edges in the graph, simplifying and speeding up scheduling. The motivation for this change was a pathological test case which was taking more than 15 minutes to compile.
    The generator also assigns weights to each node by iterating over the generated nodes, rather than trying to walk the graph.
    In SHAVEPreRAScheduler, I am replacing the recursive scheduleDependencyNode function with an iterative approach.
    Also fixing a couple of bugs in SHAVEPostRAScheduler.
    The two options for tuning scheduling have also been removed and placed into SHAVEOptions.cpp.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@109115 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

