commit 80c31698e3951963e63b1c3d278a1c773d2a7522
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 11 13:09:34 2016 +0000

    This is a huge bunch of changes for the new pre-RA and post-RA schedulers.
    In SHAVESchedulerBase, I am adding support to properly track (and ignore) dead definitions of registers. This allows instructions that implicitly modify unused condition registers to be reordered safely (e.g. IAU instructions that edit I_STATE). But it still maintains correct ordering when the register is used (e.g. IAU.ADD -> IAU.ADDCI ordering).
    I'm also removing the function getModifiedConflictSet. The pre-RA and post-RA schedulers now define their own versions of this function.
    In SHAVEPreRAScheduler, I am removing unnecessary reordering of the final schedule. It no longer accounts for the latency of instructions during the reordering step. This was causing independent and overlapping instruction chains to be reordered so that they were no longer overlapping. This meant that the register allocator was reusing the same registers in each independent chain, preventing the post-RA scheduler from overlapping them.
    I'm also adding appropriate latency for pseudo load instructions during pre-RA scheduling.
    In SHAVEPostRAScheduler, I am adding support for CMU copy to (IAU|SAU|VAU).OR instruction mutations. I am also adding IAU to SAU instruction mutations and LSU(0|1) mutations.
    The Post-RA scheduler will now schedule flow and output dependent successors of a node first, followed by anti-dependent successors (in order of weight in each case).
    I am also adding support to the post-RA scheduler for replacing BRU.JMP instructions with BRU.BRA instructions.
    The scheduler will also now honour the semantics specified by the command-line options "-shave-lsu-load-policy", "-shave-lsu-store-policy", and "-shave-no-replace-jmp-with-bra".
    This commit also includes initial support for -g with the new schedulers and also a non-optimising version of the post-RA scheduler for -O0. Neither of these have been properly tested yet.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@108676 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

