    moviCompile / mlibneon: fix vbsl in header -- attribute alias
    
    It seems that,
    "when an inline function in a header file also provides an alias, but for one reason or another if the compiler is forced to instantiate the inline function (the ‘-fno-inline-functions’ flag does this; code complexity can cause it, or taking the address of the function), then the function is placed in a special section prefixed with ‘.gnu_linkonce’ so that if there are 2 or more files which cause it to be instantiated, then the linker can discard the duplicate.
    
    This works fine until an alias is added, and it appears that the alias does not obey the same rules as the primary symbol, and the resulting program can have multiple definition errors."
    
