commit d55abd51fc97cb40681e85fe48bdc9b4eca66481
Author: Samuel Ghinet <samuel.ghinet@movidius.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 13 13:56:21 2016 +0000

    moviCompile / mlibneon tests: refactor & cleanup
    
    1. TElem and other types that can be deduced: now use auto
    2. renamed j -> vecIdx; i -> elemIdx
    3. log text update: "d" -> "actual"; "should be" -> "expected"
    4. removed TElem(variable) in MVC_PRINTF-s. It was relevant when on the arm board we were building with gcc - because the element type of e.g. int8x8_t was not an int8_t, but an alternative to it.
    5. turned operation functors (e.g. TOperation) into functions & function calls: to remove the need of explicit scalar type, and need for template.
    6. made the names of template vector types more consistent: e.g. TVecIn, TIn -> TVec
    7. renamed dElem, actualElem, etc. -> actual
    8. renamed opResult, expElem, etc. -> expected
    9. renamed the rest of parameterized test functions -> test_op, and made them non-inline.
    10. template constant "count": can be computed inside the test_op function.
    11. removed macros - except for those with CALL_N -- calling the test_op multiple times, with different compile-time constants
    12. removed doc comments for test_op - outdated, not needed, actually.
    13. declared NeonIntrinsic inside each test_op: so that no std::function will need to be passed as parameter. also, the tests which did have NeonIntrinsic, but were given as template parameters, now have the NeonIntrinsic inside the test_op also.
    14. gotten rid of get_vec_value and set_vec_value - were relevant in the times when we were building the tests on arm board with gcc.
    15. vrshl{q}_{s/u}64 - some bug fixes. will need to be revised a bit.
    16. split test_vpmin_vpmax.cpp in 2 files, and extracted vqmovn from test_vqmovun.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@100568 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

