commit c45f75395afd643c8c3c7b9e48d8fd5911114716
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 4 10:03:30 2016 +0000

    This is a big set of changes for the new instruction schedulers.
    Removing the SHAVEResourceManager. It has been replaced by the SHAVESchedulerBase which both schedulers subclass. The scheduler base defines common functionality to both schedulers. This includes SHAVECycleIterator, SHAVEDependencyNode and the schedules themselves. It contains the functions responsible for generating the dependency graphs, comparing memory accesses, and finding the start/end cycles of blocks in the schedules.
    The Pre-RA specific behaviour from SHAVEResourceManager is separated out into the SHAVEPreRAScheduler class.
    Adding the beginnings of the Post-RA scheduler. This scheduler builds traces, generates the dependency graphs for those traces and does some simple (top-down and bottom-up) scheduling of those graphs.
    Adding a new version of PEU.PCCX which mirrors the interface for PEU.PC1C except with an immediate operand for the active slots. This will allow for directly replacing a PEU.PC1C instruction with a corresponding PEU.PCCX instruction.
    Adding a "All functional units in use" conflict for inline assembly blocks.
    
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@99720 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

