commit f7ac1e83e1aeacd20a29039b58ecc9d1b07e6dea
Author: Samuel Ghinet <samuel.ghinet@movidius.com>
Date:   Wed Jun 15 13:15:28 2016 +0000

    moviCompile / mlibneon - fixes for vqdml{a/s}l_{lane/n}_<type> --- saturation for doubling
    
    explanations
    ------------
    e.g. a doubling multiply of two int16_t values, a and b.
    
    If a is 0x7fff and b is 0x7fff (max signed) => a * b is 0x3fff0001 (i.e. no saturation, extending instead).
    And the doubling of 0x3fff0001 is 0x7ffe0002  -- it does not overflow, so it doesn't saturate.
    
    BUT
    if a is 0x8000 and b is 0x8000 (minimum signed) => a * b is 0x40000000. (i.e. still, no saturation, extending instead).
    And then we have the doubling: 0x40000000 * 2 = 0x80000000 (minimum int32_t) => saturate to 0x7FFFFFFF
    
    The previous implementation did not realize the potential of the doubling to overflow.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@98308 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

