    moviCompile / mlibneon: vqdmulh bugfix - saturation not taken into account for vqdmulh{q}_s32
    
    As far as I can see, there is only one case - pair of values - that can cause saturation, for this intrinsic.
    if a[i] = b[i] = (int32_t)0x80000000 (negative value) => (a[i] * b[i]) * 2 = 0x8000000000000000LL -- which is STILL a negative.
    In this case, the result is saturated to the positive value 0x7fffffffffffffff and only the HO 32bit part is returned (0x7fffffff)
    
    Also, for some reason, the tests did not / no longer returned "1" in case of error.
    
