commit 7297258f37c1e2fd1614a4edae76d3155c337ad5
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Wed May 11 09:46:44 2016 +0000

    Improving the tracking of live registers in the pre-RA scheduler. The scheduler will now count the number of live-in virtual registers to the block for the first cycle.
    This also changes the uses of MachineOperand::isKill(). The kill flags are not necessarily maintained on entry to the scheduler so we must use the LiveIntervals to determine liveness of virtual registers.
    Also making changes to how the schedule is emitted and applied back to the basic block. Instead of removing all instructions and the re-inserting them into the block, we now simply move them around using MachineBasicBlock::splice(). This approach plays nicer with LiveIntervals.
    Fixing a bug in the anti-dependency checking when building the dependency graphs.
    Previously the experimental pre-RA scheduler was being added as an additional pass, with the original pre-RA scheduler still running as well. The experimental scheduler will now replace the original scheduler outright when the experimental scheduler enable flag has been set.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@95233 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

