Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Mon May 9 09:48:25 2016 +0000

    Fixing a bug in the use of SHAVE::PEU_PVEN8C_Myr2v1 during the custom emission of SHAVE::INSERT_SUBVECTOR_* pseudo instructions.
    Previously the instruction was being passed the destination register of the bundled CMU instruction. However, this means that before register allocation the definition of that register does not dominate all of its uses. To overcome this, we now pass the first source register to the SHAVE::PEU_PVEN8C_Myr2v1. This should not be an issue since the destination and first source registers are tied together and are guaranteed to be the same after register allocation.
    
