commit 9b993ca1dcdc707612fd98bf00c10aa29f94ba98
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Mon May 9 09:41:59 2016 +0000

    Adding more functionality to the new pre-RA instruction scheduler.
    The LSU0[0|1] conflicts have been merged into one. A new function called SHAVEResourceManager::getModifiedConflictSet performs some extra checks on the usesLSU0 and usesLSU1 conflict types to allow two LSUs to be used in a single cycle.
    Adding LSU0[0|1] conflicts to the load/store pseudo instructions in SHAVEInstrInfo.td.
    Replacing the single "-mllvm -shave-enable-experimental-scheduler" flag with two separate flags, one for the pre-RA scheduler and another for the post-RA scheduler. These new flags are "-mllvm -shave-enable-experimental-prera-scheduler" and "-mllvm -shave-enable-experimental-postra-scheduler".
    Adding a new register class to SHAVERegisterInfo.td to encapsulate the super-registers for the various combinations of CMU condition codes.
    Adding support to the SHAVE Resource Manager to track live register sets in the pre-RA scheduler. Also making big changes to how the dependency graphs are generated. The previous method was incredibly slow and clunky, this new one is much faster.
    The dependency graphs also pay attention to potential memory aliasing when being generated. The function SHAVEResourceManager::compareMemoryAccesses deals with this.
    Adding checks for anti-dependencies and output-dependencies during dependency graph generation.
    Adding support for existing bundles of instructions to the pre-RA scheduler.
    
