commit 43187833a6f2651cc9f9c21f8da54cee65b6efe4
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Thu Apr 21 09:35:56 2016 +0000

    This is the first set of changes for adding new pre-RA and post-RA instruction schedulers.
    The new schedulers can be enabled using a flag "-mllvm -shave-enable-experimental-scheduler". Although right now this will just hit an llvm_unreachable in the post-RA scheduler, which has yet to be implemented.
    The new pre-RA scheduler is able to build dependency graphs and use them to schedule basic blocks top-down. It currently only pays attention to inter-instruction dependencies and a small set of hardware conflicts.
    The brains of the operation is the new SHAVEResourceManager. It generates the dependency graphs, manages the schedules, performs conflict detection, and performs the pre-RA instruction re-ordering step. It is also able to dump the schedules in a textual format and it can dump the dependency graphs as a .dot directed graph.
    This commit also adds support for SHAVE "conflicts". Conflicts are are a new way of representing scheduling hazards. The SHAVEConflicts.td describes these conflicts. Conflicts can be described by a list of conditions called "SHAVEConflictName". These conditions can have an "all", "any", or "none" set relationship with a range of cycles. Unlike the existing hazards which are binary "Hazard" or "NoHazard", the new conflicts have a list of types associated with them. It is up to the scheduler to decide if it cares or not about individual types of hazards. This is not configurable yet, but it will be via the target.
    All of the functional unit .td changes are to add "SHAVEConflictName" conditions to appropriate instructions.
    The new TableGen generator SHAVEConflictEmitter.cpp is responsible for using these instruction tags to generate functions which identify individual conflicts that are associated with an instruction. It is also responsible for generating the function which initialises the "conflict table" used by SHAVEResourceManager to detect conflicts.
    The conflict targets, types, conditions and names are all represented by std::bitset structures.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@93591 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

