Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Mon Mar 14 10:39:39 2016 +0000

    Adding a workaround for a bug in PEU.PVEN8C on Myriad 2.1. As an example, the bundle
      PEU.PVEN8C 30 || CMU.ALIGNVEC v23 v22 v22 14
    will be replaced on Myriad 2.1 with
      PEU.PVEN8C 30 || CMU.ALIGNVEC v23 v22 v22 14 || LSU1.SWZMV8.H [7654][UUUZ] || LSU0.SWZMV8.L [3210][ZZZU] || VAU.AND v23, v23, v23
    The LSU.SWZMV8 masks are set to U for lanes disabled by the PEU.PVEN8C and to Z for lanes enabled by the PEU.PVEN8C.
    Also adding a fix for a bug in the lowering action for ShuffleAnalysis::LowerSubvectorInsert in SHAVELowering::SHAVELowerVECTOR_SHUFFLE. This was previously comparing the size of a vector in bytes with the number of elements in another. The comparison is now between the number of elements in each vector.
    In SHAVEAsmScheduler.cpp and LiveIntervalAnalysis.cpp, I'm adding a fix for a bug introduced during pre-RA scheduling that caused the live intervals for virtual registers defined in bundles to be invalid.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@89264 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

