commit 91aac715acc64bb1acd2d9389dc09c6650ec8e34
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Fri Mar 4 11:57:24 2016 +0000

    Adding an implementation for vector subvector insertion with a constant index.
    The Shuffle Analyser in SHAVELowering.cpp has been extended to match the shuffle patterns used for subvector insertion. The lowering action for these types of shuffle is to replace them with a SHAVEISD::EXTRACT_SUBVECTOR from the source and a SHAVEISD::INSERT_SUBVECTOR into the destination. If the source node happens to be a CONCAT_VECTORS node, then we are sometimes able to simply remove the appropriate subvector operand from this node at compile time and do not need to emit an EXTRACT_SUBVECTOR instruction.
    These new SHAVEISD::INSERT_SUBVECTOR nodes are selected by patterns in SHAVEInstrInfo.td and are replaced with type specific pseudo instructions. These pseudo instructions are later replaced in SHAVELowering.cpp using a custom instruction emitter (SHAVELowering::EmitCustomINSERT_SUBVECTOR).
    The changes made to the PEU and CMU td files are to add new instruction definitions to aid this implementation.
    The changes to SHAVEInstrInfo.cpp are because of the use of SHAVE::PEU_PVEN8C which does not predicate execution. Since it is a PEU instruction however, the existing implementation assumed it did.
