    moviComplie / mlibneon: fix vaba{q/l} and vabd{q/l} instructions for unsigned -- according to arm board
    
    Absolute difference for unsigned vectors works the same as for the
    signed types (i.e. the value of the difference is treated as if it were signed)
    EXCEPT -- in signed operations, for, e.g. int32x2_t, we work with 31 bits, for
    the HO bit is kept for sign, and THIS is how the 'abs' builtin knows whether to
    alter that value or not (if it is negative or not). For unsigned operations we
    work with all 32bits, which complicates things a bit.
    
    Also, the tests had to be updated -- the understanding of these instructions for
    the unsigned types were flawed, therefore the associated tests were flawed.
    
    The tests pass now both on myriad2 (with simulator) and on the beagle board (arm).
    
