commit b00bd6a41316b33ea77591bf5cd9becfee889a89
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Mon Feb 22 10:49:31 2016 +0000

    Implementing subvector extraction for SHAVE.
    This involves adding a new opcode EXTRACT_SUBVECTOR to the SHAVEISD namespace. This new opcode takes two arguments; The first is the vector to extract from, the second is the starting index of the extract. The index can be any value between 0 and the number of elements in the source vector. It can be either variable or constant.
    SHAVEISD::EXTRACT_SUBVECTOR is selected by the DAGCombiner in SHAVELowering. A chain of ISD::INSERT_VECTOR_ELT and ISD::EXTRACT_VECTOR_ELT nodes can be matched and replaced by a single SHAVEISD::EXTRACT_SUBVECTOR node. A full description of this process is described in the document "docs/Vector insert, extract and shuffle.docx".
    Next, SHAVEISD::EXTRACT_SUBVECTOR is replaced either by a sequence of Machine Instructions or by a pseudo instruction in SHAVEISelDAGtoDAG. When the index is constant, the machine instructions are selected. When the index is variable, SHAVEISelDAGtoDAG falls through to the pattern matcher which selects the pseudo instructions using their TabelGen patterns.
    These pseudo instructions are replaced by a sequence of machine instructions using a custom instruction inserter, which is called by SHAVELowering::EmitInstrWithCustomInserter.
    
    Modifying SHAVEAsmScheduler so that the pre-RA scheduler maintains instruction bundles that existed before scheduling started. This is mainly for instructions like BRU.RPI that have unique interactions with bundles.
    Adding new CMU and IAU instructions (without patterns) to facilitate the new SHAVEISD::EXTRACT_SUBVECTOR lowering.
    Also moving the special handling of ISD::INSERT_VECTOR_ELT that overcomes certain hardware bugs from SHAVELowering to SHAVEISelDAGtoDAG. This was necessary to simplify the pattern matching for SHAVISD::EXTRACT_SUBVECTOR.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@87053 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

