commit 9a7e04d872715b293fb985ea468d67c1e6f4c0c0
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Wed Feb 10 10:56:38 2016 +0000

    This is a complete overhaul of the handling of vector element insert and extract. For a full description of the code generated by these changes, look at the document "docs/Vector insert, extract and shuffle.docx".
    The nodes ISD::INSERT_VECTOR_ELT and ISD::EXTRACT_VECTOR_ELT are lowered in three different ways in the SHAVE backend.
    
    In SHAVELowering.cpp there is custom lowering for ISD::INSERT_VECTOR_ELT of i8 values with a constant index. This is necessary since these operations lower to three machine instructions. For Myriad2.1, this file also handles both constant and variable index ISD::INSERT_VECTOR_ELT of x8 and x16 values. This is because of a bug in CMU.CPIV.x16.
    SHAVELowering.cpp also contains custom lowering for ISD::EXTRACT_VECTOR_ELT of two different types. The first type is extraction from 16/32 bit vectors with a variable index, the second is extraction of x8 values from 64/128 bit vectors with a constant index. In both cases, there are >1 machine instructions required to lower the operation, so custom lowering is necessary.
    
    The following are lowered automatically using patterns from Tablegen:
    ISD::INSERT_VECTOR_ELT of x16 and x32 values into 64/128 bit vectors with a constant index
    ISD::INSERT_VECTOR_ELT of x8 and x16 values into 16/32 bit vectors with a constant index
    ISD::EXTRACT_VECTOR_ELT of x32 and x16 values from 64/128 bit vectors with a constant index
    ISD::EXTRACT_VECTOR_ELT of x8 and x16 from 16/32 bit vectors with a constant index
    
    The third and final way, SHAVEISelDAGtoDAG.cpp handles all other types using CMU.LUT for ISD::EXTRACT_VECTOR_ELT and CMU.LUTW for ISD::INSERT_VECTOR_ELT. In the SHAVE/SHAVEAsmScheduler.cpp, these operations are expanded to LUT pseudo instructions which take an extra input register that is used later as a temporary intermediate register for setting up the LUT index operand. These pseudo instructions are expanded after register allocation in SHAVEArrayPromotion.cpp.
    
    This overhaul removes the need for the SHAVEISD::VROT_MYR1 and SHAVEISD::VROT_MYR2 operations, so they have been removed. Several unusable variants of CMU_CPVI have also been removed.
    
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@86174 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

