commit 12aa383fed65f0fb272f819fa2970b4fabe1e5c5
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Thu Dec 3 13:30:41 2015 +0000

    Adding support for BRU.RPI and BRU.RPIM. moviCompile will now optimise some small loops to use BRU.RPI.
    Simple "while(1);" loops will be optimised to "BRU.RPIM 0".
    BRU.RPI[M] instructions are inserted into BasicBlocks in SHAVEInstrInfo.cpp, during the expansion of the pseudo instructions SHAVE::JMP_TO_LABEL and SHAVE::JMPcc_TO_LABEL.
    The changes made to SHAVEAsmScheduler.cpp are to prevent the scheduler from removing instructions from/inserting instructions into existing BRU.RPI bundles. BRU.RPI is a "special" case that needs to be handled differently to other instructions.
    Similar changes were required in SHAVESuperBlock.cpp to prevent it merging a BasicBlock into another containing a BRU.RPI bundle.
    
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@83291 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

