commit 5e4d127061e7b1423d225e4226feb6e4e4487709
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 24 11:20:55 2015 +0000

    This is a big set of fixes for handling debug information properly in the SHAVE backend at optimisation levels -O1 and above.
    This fixes bug #23239 and bug #23240 (and removes the predicated NOPs seen in bug #23238).
    The changes made to SHAVEAsmPrinter.cpp fixes bug #23240. With NOP compression disabled, individual NOPs were being emitted at a different point in the compilation process than when NOP compression was enabled. Now, NOPs are always emitted at the same point, with and without NOP compression enabled. They are emitted before predication takes place on instruction bundles. (This also removes the predicated NOPs seen in bug #23238).
    The changes to SHAVEAsmScheduler.cpp, SHAVEHazardRecognizer.cpp, SHAVEPredicator.cpp and SHAVELatencyPass.cpp are primarily just adding checks for either "isPosition", "isDebugValue" or "isCFIInstriction" where they were previously missing.
    SHAVEPeepHoleOptimization.cpp was incorrectly treating debug information as instructions when determining whether or not it is safe to replace a BRU.JMP with a BRU.BRA. Debug information is now no longer counted as an instruction.
    Two new functions called "removeDebugInfo" and "reinsertDebugInfo" have been added to SHAVESuperBlock.cpp. This is to fix the issues shown in bug #23239. When merging basic blocks (and filling branch delay slots), the super block scheduler was incorrectly treating debug information as regular machine instructions. The debug information is just noise to SHAVESuperBlock and is not required at all. As such, debug information is now completely removed from the DAG before SHAVESuperBlock is run. Once the super block scheduling has been completed, the debug information is reinserted into the DAG. Positional information is maintained for each instruction when being removed. This means that each piece of debug information is essentially tied to a specific machine instruction. If that machine instruction is moved, then so is the corresponding debug information.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@82956 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

