commit a163bb39c313be95af6c5a4ab05007e5d25f25c6
Author: Martin J. O'Riordan <martin.oriordan@movidius.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 08:26:33 2015 +0000

    Fixing a regression in the calling-convention handling when the argument type is 'float2'.
    
    This fix will be available in "v00.50.70.0 Alpha #2" of 'moviCompile' at the next Alpha release cycle, or in "v00.50.68.2" if we do patch release.
    
    The workaround is to pass these as 'float4' from C/C++.  In assembler there is no need to change to use this workaround.
    
    So for example, if you have:
    
      extern void foo(float2);
      float2 f2 = { 1.0f, 2.0f };
      foo(f2);
    
    then rewrite this as:
    
      extern void foo(float4);
      float4 f4 = { 0.0f, 0.0f, 1.0f, 2.0f };
      foo(f4);
    
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@81719 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

