commit 7183681e63e4523d59b2b75fc975c3f0fe20ca6f
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 17:14:36 2015 +0000

    Completely overhauling SHAVEInstrInfo::copyPhysReg. It is now only possible to copy between registers of the same size. This has had several knock-on effects on the rest of the backend. Specifically on sections that were emitting instructions that used/produced registers of different sizes to what was actually expected. This caused implicit TARGETISD::COPY instructions between registers of different sizes (which is not legal).
    SHAVEInstrInfo, SHAVEISelDAGtoDAG and SHAVELowering have been modified to use appropriately sized sub-registers in place of the old default IRF32 and VRF128.
    This has a knock-on effect on SHAVEInstrInfo_CMU.td, SHAVEInstrInfo_IAU.td, and SHAVEInstrInfo_VAU.td, which now have new sub-register variants of pre-existing instructions.
    SHAVEAsmScheduler has been modified to mutate all variants of CMU_CP instructions into LSU_CP instructions where appropriate. This also had a knock-on effect on SHAVEInstrInfo_LSU.td, which now has new LSU_CP variants.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@79422 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

