commit de062c2ebc1d8058ba90276ca0ca9ab3d0a151e7
Author: Martin J. O'Riordan <martin.oriordan@movidius.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 27 12:51:12 2015 +0000

    The 'f16_h' variants of the intrinsics are not supported on Myriad1.
    The reason for this is that in order to support them, the compiler needs to be able to copy an 'SRF16_l' to an 'SRF16_h'.  The 'CMU.CPSS' instruction does not have a suitable variants, nor is it possible to use a shift of CMBBYTE operation on an SRF.  The only way of doing this would be to copy to an IRF, then shift, then copy back to an IRF.  This sequence is too expensive to be worth implementing, and will never occur in any context other than through the use of these intrinsic.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@78102 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

