commit 933df5bd81762d291d149d4a7655b1020e81b1a3
Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 16 09:52:31 2015 +0000

    Fix for bug #22208. While expanding the pseudo-instruction INPUT_SWIZZLE8, the compiler would only search the instruction's parent Basic Block for its first user. INPUT_SWIZZLE8 is a representation of LSU.SWZ instructions, so the first user of the pseudo-instruction is the CMU/VAU/SAU instruction that the LSU.SWZ should be bundled with. The bug was being caused by LLVM "sinking" the user instruction into a successor of the pseudo-instruction's parent Basic Block. Since the compiler was only searching the parent Basic Block, it could not find the user instruction. This has been changed now so that it searches the successors of the parent Basic Block which have the result register of the INPUT_SWIZZLE8 marked as "Live In".
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@76130 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

