Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Fri May 29 09:38:20 2015 +0000

    Fix for bug #21973. Since there was no specific handling for v2i32 in the SHAVE backend, LLVM was using the patterns for i64 values to load/store v2i32. This meant that v2i32 vectors were being placed into IRF register pairs, rather than halves of VRF registers. This commit adds explicit support for v2i32 in the backend, using halves of VRF registers.
    16 bit parts of VRF registers (VRF_e0..7) have been enabled to support this.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@75150 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

