Author: Stephen Rogers <stephen.rogers@movidius.com>
Date:   Mon May 25 09:10:35 2015 +0000

    Minor fix for a bug introduced into the SLP vectoriser during the v3.6 merge. The bug was causing many of the TSVC tests to fail during compilation.
    Also a fix for the INPUT_SWIZZLE8 pseudo instruction. This instruction is primarily used as a representation of LSU.SWZ8 instructions, which swizzle the result of a VAU/CMU/SAU vector operation. Since the instructions are "tied together" by their use operands (and not the result of the swizzle), there was an issue with registers being unintentionally renamed. By requiring the $dst and $src registers be the same, the register defined by the operation is the same as the used register. This means that a normal def-use relationship exists between the two operations.
    
    git-svn-id: http://dub30/svn/TRUNK/Compilers/moviCompile@74821 1056b6a0-8826-0410-81dd-e2f0166d4647

