    Three sets of changes here:
    
      o  Adding support for the various names for the Myriad
         processors: ma1100, ma2100, etc.
      o  Predefining:
           _LIBCPP_HAS_NO_THREADS
           _LIBCPP_HAS_NO_MONOTONIC_CLOCK
         and conditionally predefining:
           _LIBCPP_NO_RTTI
         if '-fno-rtti' is selected.  These are necessary to
         ensure that the C++ library behaves correctly for SHAVE
         and removes the need for the customer to remember to
         add them.
      o  Adding an experimental hidden option to permit non-ASM
         in the body of 'naked' functions.  This was permitted
         by CLang v3.5 but explicitly forbidden in v3.6.  Even
         though we officially do NOT support this attribute,
         there are customers who apparently use it.
    
    However, I may revert the last change, as it appears that CLang and/or LLVM is assuming that this cannot happen as the compiler asserts and crashes in several places when C code is added to a 'naked' function.
    
